{"name":"Forest Green","hex":"#154406","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Forest Green","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A place name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Forest_Green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Forest Green, Oh Forest Green","blocks":[{"text":"Forest Green, Oh Forest Green is the first single by American singer-songwriter Holly Miranda from her album The Magician's Private Library, released 9 November 2009 in the UK and 17 November 2009 in the United States by XL Recordings. It was co-written and features guest vocals by musician Brendan Coon."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Forest_Green%2C_Oh_Forest_Green.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest_Green%2C_Oh_Forest_Green","wikidata":"Q5468880"},{"title":"Forest green","blocks":[{"text":"Forest green is a representation of the average color of the leaves of the trees of a temperate zone deciduous forest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Forest_Green_%289674379239%29.jpg/330px-Forest_Green_%289674379239%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest_green","wikidata":"Q17105502"},{"title":"Forest","blocks":[{"text":"A forest is an ecosystem characterized by a dense community of trees. Hundreds of definitions of forest are used throughout the world, incorporating factors such as tree density, tree height, land use, legal standing, and ecological function. The United Nations' Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) defines a forest as, \"Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban use.\" Using this definition, Global Forest Resources Assessment 2025 found that forests covered 4.14 billion hectares, or approximately 31 percent of the world's land area in 2025."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg/330px-Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest","wikidata":"Q4421"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Forest_Green%2C_Oh_Forest_Green.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Forest_Green%2C_Oh_Forest_Green.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AForest_Green%2C_Oh_Forest_Green.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Forest_Green_%289674379239%29.jpg/500px-Forest_Green_%289674379239%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Forest_Green_%289674379239%29.jpg/1280px-Forest_Green_%289674379239%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Forest_Green_%289674379239%29.jpg/500px-Forest_Green_%289674379239%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ferns in a forest","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AForest_Green_(9674379239).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg/500px-Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg/1280px-Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&